From 50153aaad7d3468c8926fc9228273dba049ab274 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:52:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 95/95] doc/examples/transcode_aac: return a plain exit status

main() returned its internal status, AVERROR_EXIT, on every failure.
That is a large negative number, so the process exit status was its low
byte, 187, whatever went wrong. Return 1 on failure and 0 on success
like the other examples do (transcode.c uses "ret ? 1 : 0").

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FZ4G6798n6Ua4qu6xwWu3S
---
 doc/examples/transcode_aac.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/doc/examples/transcode_aac.c b/doc/examples/transcode_aac.c
index b7a59adff8..39dd456ebf 100644
--- a/doc/examples/transcode_aac.c
+++ b/doc/examples/transcode_aac.c
@@ -944,5 +944,5 @@ cleanup:
     if (input_format_context)
         avformat_close_input(&input_format_context);
 
-    return ret;
+    return ret ? 1 : 0;
 }
